{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut","id":1518037,"title":"Explanation why Fenrir were cut","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-15T08:45:25-07:00","id":1518037,"title":"Explanation why Fenrir were cut","content":"<img width=\"666\" height=\"888\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I uhh, what? Not only are ahroun VERY different from the Fenrir, but the Fenrir also are one of the closest to the 'expected' type of werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T09:22:38-07:00","id":1518040,"title":"","content":"And silly me belived for three decades, one of the Garou's biggest tragedy was to be fractured in to Tribes with distinct culture and charactersitics and Patrons. This is the source most of their problem, they are not an united people.<br /> &quot;Werewolves&quot; yes, but different flavour of them... abandoned Old Wolf of the Woods and weaseled their way in to the favor of other Spirits for power (and some cases they even abandon those to, Sasquatch\u200b for Wendigo (I know, I know, truth behind the disappearance is, Sasquatch <i>is</i> Wendigo. Forever changed by the journey to the Pure Lands. The Wendigo, with the assistance of this new, ferocious spirit propered but they don't really know the truth...) in the case of the Wendigo, or left Crow for first Susanowo (if you belive that tale) then Grandfather Thunder in the case of the Lords....<br /> And this is the tragic and &quot;human&quot; part...<br /> I was a fool...<br /> Woe me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-15-2023, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T09:24:42-07:00","id":1518041,"title":"","content":"So this was just more of Achilli rewriting the setting to remove any elements he and the others at Paradox consider to be &quot;badwrongfun&quot; again? Can't say I'm surprised by this at all.<br /> <br /> Shame, because I liked the Get of Fenris. Still do. They're tied with Glass Walkers for my favorite tribe.<br /> <br /> Guess I'm still going to be sticking to W20 (or even Werewolf 2e)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T09:43:31-07:00","id":1518042,"title":"","content":"That's why I said in the other thread that I personally think this could be another remnant from the first iteration developed by Hunter instead considering how the Get were portrayed in the Heart of the Forest game. Because if you go with the version JA has been talking about since last October his explanation has always been that the developers essentially couldn't come up with verbs for the Get Tribe that were distinct from the Ahroun-Auspice. And let's not forget what the verbs for Ahroun are: Fight, Attack, Destroy, Charge. First, you got a rather bland selection of verbs for Ahroun there and then you got the argument that supposedly no one could come up with a distinct set of verbs for a W5 version of Get. It's a bit... weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:54:38-07:00","id":1518055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518042#post1518042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I said in the other thread that I personally think this could be another remnant from the first iteration developed by Hunter instead considering how the Get were portrayed in the Heart of the Forest game. Because if you go with the version JA has been talking about since last October his explanation has always been that the developers essentially couldn't come up with verbs for the Get Tribe that were distinct from the Ahroun-Auspice. And let's not forget what the verbs for Ahroun are: Fight, Attack, Destroy, Charge. First, you got a rather bland selection of verbs for Ahroun there and then you got the argument that supposedly no one could come up with a distinct set of verbs for a W5 version of Get. It's a bit... weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really weird and really like no one even tried. Not exactly the blink of an eye, but: Determine, Endure, Halt, Terrify. This is leaning hard on the interpretation of their being about grim resolve, brutal chiminage that inures them to the feelings of injury, pinning down annoyingly quick foes, and, of course, being able to cow others with the sight of their fangs bared. This is distinct from what they interpret as Ahroun because it centers around day to day life and being toughened by their harsh home.<br /> <br /> Dunno what the problem was. I'd be more worried about being redundant with the Galestalkers, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T11:10:30-07:00","id":1518058,"title":"","content":"Hmm....<br /> <br /> I'm not the biggest Get fan in the world (I'm more of a Wendigo girl), but this confirms my suspicions that the current 5th Ed design teams aren't very imaginative. The design decisions with this current edition just perplex me, as they seem to be trying to increase variety while contradictorily limiting it.<br /> <br /> It's a reason why I don't really want to venture out of 20th Anniversary Editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T11:11:14-07:00","id":1518059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518055#post1518055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds really weird and really like no one even tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows what was going on with the development here... Like, let's not forget: A core-part of the redesign was severing the link between human ethnicity/culture and the Tribes but then you got the infamous &quot;Fianna is just a word&quot;-comment from JA. Or even that comment up there... The design-idea according to the dev-blog-posts is &quot;Tribe is what you do, Auspice is how you do it.&quot;. If like this explanation claims you come up with the <i>same </i>answer for &quot;What do you do?&quot; and &quot;How do you do it?&quot; then I wouldn't think that the Get-Tribe is the issue here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518055#post1518055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly the blink of an eye, but: Determine, Endure, Halt, Terrify. This is leaning hard on the interpretation of their being about grim resolve, brutal chiminage that inures them to the feelings of injury, pinning down annoyingly quick foes, and, of course, being able to cow others with the sight of their fangs bared. This is distinct from what they interpret as Ahroun because it centers around day to day life and being toughened by their harsh home.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thanks to the previews we already know what the actual write-up for the Auspice in the book is like... It ends with the inspired line &quot;Fuck you, Wyrm.&quot;, so tonally they go for a bit less circumspect interpretation there, it seems...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T12:39:09-07:00","id":1518062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut#post1518037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img width=\"666\" height=\"888\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever. I'm not buying his explanations and I'm <b><u>definitely</u></b> not buying his werewolf-related &quot;product.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T12:48:55-07:00","id":1518065,"title":"","content":"I mean....that's an obvious lie. For a start you could easily generate other tribes as antagonists like they did with forsaken which would enrich the setting rather than diminish it.<br /> <br /> Honestly between justin and khelil I'm beginning to prefer the silent treatment.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit-as a side if anyone can be a viking. No ones a viking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-15-2023, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:50:21-07:00","id":1518077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518062#post1518062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever. I'm not buying his explanations and I'm <b><u>definitely</u></b> not buying his werewolf-related &quot;product.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same here.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to mince words here, Justin Achilli has been trying to force everyone to play Vampire the &quot;One True Way&quot; and to tell all naysayers to go play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; since at least 1999 with VTM Revised, but seeing him do the same thing to Werewolf, the game that always presented itself as a game of savage action-horror from the very beginning is just baffling. You'd think Achilli would pass on Werewolf and try to tackle Wraith 5E instead (or at least Mage since that one was more popular) but him, Kareem, and the rest of the Paradox/Renegade crew doing this to Werewolf feels especially vindictive.<br /> <br /> At least Vampire 1E had the &quot;Storytelling Game of Personal Horror&quot; rhetoric as a marketing gimmick to get more people from outside the usual gaming hobby demographics to buy the game (a gimmick that paid off big time)<br /> <br /> Let's be honest with ourselves here, the first edition of VTM was very much the &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas/Supers With Fangs&quot; badwrongfun that Achilli infamously hates despite all the corebook window dressing that would say otherwise, and the second edition of VTM was like that to an even greater degree.<br /> <br /> Both were better games for it, IMHO, but that's just personal opinion.<br /> <br /> With Vampire, you could at least make an argument that Justin Achilli wanted to bring that game to be more in line with the taglines, rhetoric, and fluff of the first two editions' corebooks and he has been at least trying to doing that with every iteration of Vampire he worked on with the exception of V20, and this includes his work for Requiem as well.<br /> <br /> I don't know what they were thinking when they decided to let Achilli do Werewolf. You think Paradox would've got someone like Ethan Skemp to head up W5 instead but I guess not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 07-15-2023, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T15:59:07-07:00","id":1518094,"title":"","content":"There's actually a follow up to that.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1326\" height=\"191\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:11:23-07:00","id":1518097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518094#post1518094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a follow up to that.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1326\" height=\"191\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so; Bitten werewolf, cursed werewolf, born werewolf, werewolf through ritual, spiritual werewolf, knight werewolf, hell diving demon slayer werewolf and many more. There are plenty of werewolves found in pop culture and fiction, if you just bother to look.<br /> <br /> On top of everything, as I have stated many times, the garou aren't even the typical pop culture werewolves. So that statement is false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:23:05-07:00","id":1518099,"title":"","content":"Werewolf already had LOTS of internal antagonists that provided direct and immediate conflict. That got downplayed in Revised in favor of heroic fantasy when everyone was expected to team up under the signature NPCs to follow the metaplot, but you just need to examine the original books to get an idea of what is out there. There was no need to designate one of the Garou tribes as the enemy (and if you want that, there is already the Black Spiral Dancers so you're just duplicating an existing conflict, not giving the ST a new tool).<br /> <br /> First, there was already a lot of legitimate conflicts between the various tribes based on the nature of their totems, the typical tribal approaches to problems, and historical grievances. These exist primarily so the PCs can help the Garou rise above them and concentrate on the real enemy, but if the ST wants they can become a major issue in a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Second, there is internal competition for the scarce resources between Garou - cubs, kinfolk, and caerns are all being fought after, stolen, or conquered.<br /> <br /> Third, there is the Ronin - a big mass of rejected, unaligned, or lost Garou. You can do something with them. You don't even need to transform all Ronin into being something specific. You just need a particular group (or groups) of them to do something that causes issues.<br /> <br /> Fourth, every tribe had a camp that was clearly intended to be antagonists to the rest of the tribe and the Garou Nation as a whole.<br /> <br /> Fifth, you can play up the issue of man eating. It must be in the Litany for a reason. And there is no reason to limit it to the Man Eaters camp of the Bone Gnawers, though they are the largest and most organized group.<br /> <br /> Sixth, there are all sorts of secret antagonists described throughout the books that have gotten very little attention. Ever since Hakaken was introduced as a pack totem for the Black Spiral Dancers, we know there are cults of Shadow Lords who worship him. But what are these cults like? What about various totems that aren't exactly Wyrm tainted, but are heavily distrusted by the Garou. For that matter, what about even legitimate Totems like Bear whose followers get hit hard? Why can't that be showcased, or have various packs of Bears get together to do something in response? Show us exactly why packs of Bears are distrusted thousands of years after the War of Rage when other totems don't have the same problem.<br /> <br /> Seventh, you had differences in points of views between the different breeds.<br /> <br /> Eighth, the game has a long tradition of occasional Garou &quot;prophets&quot; who arrive spouting prophecies, challenges, claims to authority, call to action, and so on. A spiritual leader creating a movement to do so something can lead to lots of conflict.<br /> <br /> I can go on. If you want more internal conflict, it's all there without the need to delegitimize any of the existing tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:26:06-07:00","id":1518100,"title":"","content":"Yeah it\u2019s curious because I feel it gets to an interesting tension within most of the WoD Gamelines except Vampire. Vampire I think is the only one where you can clearly draw a through line from pre-existing literature/lore into the gameline itself, although that said the Anne Rice Vampire Chronicles themselves aren\u2019t much older than VtM but one can draw a fairly clear through line from Dracula, Carmilla, &amp; other Victorian Gothic Horror vampires.<br /> <br /> That said, none of the other Gamelines really line up that well with their popular depictions outside the WoD. While they all have certain inspirations and common attributes they\u2019re also pretty clearly their own thing. Now I think invoking real world inspirations more often would be cool, but I don\u2019t really see how you could make any WoD gameline (again, except maybe Vampire) without accepting as one of your first principles that they don\u2019t neatly correspond to inspirational material surrounding their central figures.<br /> <br /> I dunno, seems like a not great first principle to bring to the table for designing Werewolf, but it\u2019s also possible I\u2019m not fully understanding what J. Achilli &amp; co. were meaning to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:58:13-07:00","id":1518106,"title":"","content":"Double post for some reason so I deleted it. I think I actually posted a second response quoting someone that fell into the spam filter, but that did not show up but my first post. Strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-17-2023, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:23:53-07:00","id":1518107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518094#post1518094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a follow up to that.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1326\" height=\"191\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Erm those arnt mythic archeotypes, those are pop culture concepts. Mythic vampires are fragmented accounts of peasants folklore which we've wedged together because we like classifications and are no were near deep enough to build a setting from.<br /> <br /> And in the end their isn't any obligation to write your setting lore under any meta presumptions of what a fictional monster is supposed to be. That's why Stephanie myer lives in a mansion despite some nerd thinking him saying Edward wasn't a real vampire was a sick burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-16-2023, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:28:51-07:00","id":1518108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518097#post1518097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay so; Bitten werewolf, cursed werewolf, born werewolf, werewolf through ritual, spiritual werewolf, knight werewolf, hell diving demon slayer werewolf and many more. There are plenty of werewolves found in pop culture and fiction, if you just bother to look.<br /> <br /> On top of everything, as I have stated many times, the garou aren't even the typical pop culture werewolves. So that statement is false.</div> </div> </div> </div>W:tA necessarily restricts some of those because they're all born werewolves, but what we have are still pretty damn numerous. I don't really know if it's necessary to make all the splats of every game according to the same rubric of Vampire, anyway; the only reason that's even being considered is because everything is being ironed flat to make it V5 with a slightly different flavor of personal horror, even if the original game was about something else entirely.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one who kind of considers those Clan delineations kind of shallow and pieces of vampire characters that have typically had more than one? Like, Count Orlok of Nosferatu fame was definitely also an aristocrat in addition to being ugly and also bestial in that he was compared to a plague rat. So, really, just spinning off of one type of werewolf should be perfectly fine (as shown in how easy it was to derive verbs for the Fenrir).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:30:24-07:00","id":1518109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518099#post1518099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf already had LOTS of internal antagonists that provided direct and immediate conflict. That got downplayed in Revised in favor of heroic fantasy when everyone was expected to team up under the signature NPCs to follow the metaplot, but you just need to examine the original books to get an idea of what is out there. There was no need to designate one of the Garou tribes as the enemy (and if you want that, there is already the Black Spiral Dancers so you're just duplicating an existing conflict, not giving the ST a new tool).<br /> <br /> First, there was already a lot of legitimate conflicts between the various tribes based on the nature of their totems, the typical tribal approaches to problems, and historical grievances. These exist primarily so the PCs can help the Garou rise above them and concentrate on the real enemy, but if the ST wants they can become a major issue in a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Second, there is internal competition for the scarce resources between Garou - cubs, kinfolk, and caerns are all being fought after, stolen, or conquered.<br /> <br /> Third, there is the Ronin - a big mass of rejected, unaligned, or lost Garou. You can do something with them. You don't even need to transform all Ronin into being something specific. You just need a particular group (or groups) of them to do something that causes issues.<br /> <br /> Fourth, every tribe had a camp that was clearly intended to be antagonists to the rest of the tribe and the Garou Nation as a whole.<br /> <br /> Fifth, you can play up the issue of man eating. It must be in the Litany for a reason. And there is no reason to limit it to the Man Eaters camp of the Bone Gnawers, though they are the largest and most organized group.<br /> <br /> Sixth, there are all sorts of secret antagonists described throughout the books that have gotten very little attention. Ever since Hakaken was introduced as a pack totem for the Black Spiral Dancers, we know there are cults of Shadow Lords who worship him. But what are these cults like? What about various totems that aren't exactly Wyrm tainted, but are heavily distrusted by the Garou. For that matter, what about even legitimate Totems like Bear whose followers get hit hard? Why can't that be showcased, or have various packs of Bears get together to do something in response? Show us exactly why packs of Bears are distrusted thousands of years after the War of Rage when other totems don't have the same problem.<br /> <br /> Seventh, you had differences in points of views between the different breeds.<br /> <br /> Eighth, the game has a long tradition of occasional Garou &quot;prophets&quot; who arrive spouting prophecies, challenges, claims to authority, call to action, and so on. A spiritual leader creating a movement to do so something can lead to lots of conflict.<br /> <br /> I can go on. If you want more internal conflict, it's all there without the need to delegitimize any of the existing tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's like how the Camarilla used to be a powerful organization that was rumored to have tentacles everywhere, but now in V5 it's a weak and feeble thing that's turned Amish because it can't even manage a decent cyber security team. And, oh, all the Elders have run off from everywhere because mysterious metaplot reasons that'll probably never be touched on.<br /> <br /> I don't think these people are very imaginative or understand any of the material they're writing about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:33:04-07:00","id":1518110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518107#post1518107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm those arnt mythic archeotypes, those are pop culture concepts. Mythic vampires are fragmented accounts of peasants folklore which we've wedged together because we like classifications and are no were near deep enough to build a setting from.<br /> <br /> And in the end their isn't any obligation to wrote your setting lore under any meta presumptions of what a fictional monster is supposed to be. That's why Stephanie myer lives in a mansion despite some nerd thinking him saying Edward wasn't a real vampire was a sick burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a good reason that we don't stick together werewolves and vampires in the WoD even though lots of peasant folklore doesn't put such a hard line on it: that wasn't the kind of monster that the creators wanted to talk about, and later contributors didn't want to, either. End of story, or it would be, if not for the regular resurgence of people incensed that W:tA doesn't perfectly reproduce Universal Wolfman or what have you (V:tM's inability to perfectly reproduce Dracula or Nosferatu always conspicuously absent from these theses, as talking about that instantly causes the argument to crumble).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:41:24-07:00","id":1518113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518110#post1518110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also a good reason that we don't stick together werewolves and vampires in the WoD even though lots of peasant folklore doesn't put such a hard line on it: that wasn't the kind of monster that the creators wanted to talk about, and later contributors didn't want to, either. End of story, or it would be, if not for the regular resurgence of people incensed that W:tA doesn't perfectly reproduce Universal Wolfman or what have you (V:tM's inability to perfectly reproduce Dracula or Nosferatu always conspicuously absent from these theses, as talking about that instantly causes the argument to crumble).</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yeah, dracula is implied to be an evil satanic wizard with his vamparism as a product of that in the book. The neat categorisation of monsters into archeotypes is weak in pop culture and becomes farcical in folklore. <br /> <br /> If you're going to get really puritan both are supposed to be antagonists who only really exists in the context of conflict with humanity so shouldn't be played if we're maintaining some sort of pretence of historical authenticity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T18:05:54-07:00","id":1518116,"title":"","content":"Okay, this is a bit of a conspiracy-theory but this is theoretically what I could envision happened here:<ul><li>We got that version of W5 headed by Hunters Entertainment but that iteration (for whatever reason) falls apart (maybe we're gonna find out more in the future about what exactly happened here...).</li> <li>Then we got the next attempt at W5 headed by JA.</li> <li>What this development-team wanted to do is something along the same lines as H5: The game is called WtA but it's a personal horror street-level gothic punk game where you play werewolves but you are <i>not </i>playing a Garou and Garou are <i>not </i>part of the setting.</li> <li>Then Paradox told them that they wanted them to develop something closer to V5: It's an update but it's still <i>recognizable </i>as being in the same vein as those previous editions.</li> <li>This new development-team, though, really didn't like the idea of revisiting old WtA-lore and dealing with legacy-elements from previous editions.</li> <li>So what we got is this stitched-together version of old legacy-elements from previous WtA-editions, the Hunter-version's attempts at &quot;updating&quot; the setting (like V5 did) and bits and pieces of what the new team actually wanted this game to be.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T22:48:37-07:00","id":1518128,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't describe that as a conspiracy theory. It seems more of a reasonable reconstruction of what went on behind the scenes based on what limited information we know about the drastic clash in the writing thus far, 11th hour renaming of the Fianna, and continued insistence that the Get were unworkable with the complete power of retcon in the team's hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T23:33:50-07:00","id":1518129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518116#post1518116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this is a bit of a conspiracy-theory but this is theoretically what I could envision happened here:<ul><li>We got that version of W5 headed by Hunters Entertainment but that iteration (for whatever reason) falls apart (maybe we're gonna find out more in the future about what exactly happened here...).</li> <li>Then we got the next attempt at W5 headed by JA.</li> <li>What this development-team wanted to do is something along the same lines as H5: The game is called WtA but it's a personal horror street-level gothic punk game where you play werewolves but you are <i>not </i>playing a Garou and Garou are <i>not </i>part of the setting.</li> <li>Then Paradox told them that they wanted them to develop something closer to V5: It's an update but it's still <i>recognizable </i>as being in the same vein as those previous editions.</li> <li>This new development-team, though, really didn't like the idea of revisiting old WtA-lore and dealing with legacy-elements from previous editions.</li> <li>So what we got is this stitched-together version of old legacy-elements from previous WtA-editions, the Hunter-version's attempts at &quot;updating&quot; the setting (like V5 did) and bits and pieces of what the new team actually wanted this game to be.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add these;<ul><li>The BNS version was already planned and made AND we saw hints of it in Changing Ways. Then the Controversy happened in V5 and that idea was sacked.</li> <li>Hunter version went nowhere(??) and so they decided to do it in-house. That seemed to drag on as well.</li> <li>W5 was already lagging behind the schedule and so they brought in JA and basically took all the pieces from previous versions+JA's own thoughts on WtA and made our current W5.</li> <li>Because W5 HAD to come out, Rabid Black Dog was basically forced to speedrun all his art.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Please note: I do not blame the people working on W5 for the delay or am saying they are bad writers. Just that I personally feel the game currently seems disjointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T23:50:31-07:00","id":1518130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518129#post1518129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd add these;<ul><li>The BNS version was already planned and made AND we saw hints of it in Changing Ways. Then the Controversy happened in V5 and that idea was sacked.</li> <li>Hunter version went nowhere(??) and so they decided to do it in-house. That seemed to drag on as well.</li> <li>W5 was already lagging behind the schedule and so they brought in JA and basically took all the pieces from previous versions+JA's own thoughts on WtA and made our current W5.</li> <li>Because W5 HAD to come out, Rabid Black Dog was basically forced to speedrun all his art.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Please note: I do not blame the people working on W5 for the delay or am saying they are bad writers. Just that I personally feel the game currently seems disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh and some other elements that aren't exactly helpful for the development of W5 here:<ul><li>At some point post-release of H5, Justin Achilli decides to leave. That switch to his new job in January 2023 didn't happen overnight, I would assume.</li> <li>Also at some point early in 2022 while developing this version of W5, the WOD-dev-team decided to be more hands-on with the development of the V5 Players Guide (instead of just letting Renegade handle everything) and so that book got delayed while the WOD-team worked on that then as well.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T23:52:44-07:00","id":1518131,"title":"","content":"Paradox getting the rights to World of Darkness was a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T01:17:11-07:00","id":1518133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518131#post1518131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox getting the rights to World of Darkness was a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, people often look at the guys on the ground floor for blame but you usually need to look upstairs for guidance. Its pretty obvious paradox is only interested in video game spin offs. The only issue is if its bad calls filtering down or if they're not providing guidance (maybe both,).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T01:34:49-07:00","id":1518134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518133#post1518133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, people often look at the guys on the ground floor for blame but you usually need to look upstairs for guidance. Its pretty obvious paradox is only interested in video game spin offs. The only issue is if its bad calls filtering down or if they're not providing guidance (maybe both,).</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the reason, the IP hasn't been handled well. You started with V5 but then almost immediately you had a controversy and there was some shuffling around of who developed what book for the RPGs. Then Bloodlines 2 which was supposed to be the tentpole-release for the videogame-side of things had various people leaving and the project just lingering in development-hell. Then the W5-project with Hunters Entertainment fell apart. And we're sitting here years later and somehow it feels like the WOD5E project is <i>still </i>playing catch-up to get back on track with the upcoming W5-release and the announcement of more Bloodlines 2 news in a couple of months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T11:26:49-07:00","id":1518147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518133#post1518133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, people often look at the guys on the ground floor for blame but you usually need to look upstairs for guidance. Its pretty obvious paradox is only interested in video game spin offs. The only issue is if its bad calls filtering down or if they're not providing guidance (maybe both,).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it works that way, in my view Paradox just bought it for the rights and to be able to make the material they wanted, otherwise I think they wanted to leave it as it is except for the parts that could cause problems. I don't even think it's sloppiness, more lack of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T14:23:13-07:00","id":1518154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518147#post1518147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if it works that way, in my view Paradox just bought it for the rights and to be able to make the material they wanted, otherwise I think they wanted to leave it as it is except for the p<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">arts that could cause problems. I don't even thi</span>nk it's sloppiness, more lack of interest.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh, they will become interested in it once someone at the top requests some hard numbers regarding the IP's performance over the past few years and they will be of the red variety (because, seriously, this sequence of failures that is WoD5 cannot go on forever). I just hope that when it happens Paradox will wish to recuperate their losses by selling the IP to anyone, preferably someone who cares.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T15:06:37-07:00","id":1518156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518154#post1518154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh, they will become interested in it once someone at the top requests some hard numbers regarding the IP's performance over the past few years and they will be of the red variety (because, seriously, this sequence of failures that is WoD5 cannot go on forever). I just hope that when it happens Paradox will wish to recuperate their losses by selling the IP to anyone, preferably someone who cares.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Worse than that, if sales are really low, I think they will prefer to stop producing any material simply because it is not giving a financial return, or to reduce the investment until it doesn't work anymore, unless someone manages to get them out of that hole, the W5's rush could be why, the boss demanding and someone desperate who doesn't want to lose their job taking a desperate attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T01:39:56-07:00","id":1518172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518147#post1518147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if it works that way, in my view Paradox just bought it for the rights and to be able to make the material they wanted, otherwise I think they wanted to leave it as it is except for the parts that could cause problems. I don't even think it's sloppiness, more lack of interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect they're genrally sending down no controversy requests(I'm pretty confident that's why Sabbat are what they arnt in v5) as well as maybe providing unrealistic deadlines. On some level they're probably annoyed that Martin era white wolf antics forced them to get more involved.<br /> <br /> In terms of lack of interest thats definatly plausable. Considering their interest is in video games (i mean look at bloodhunt and justice). It's telling they didn't step in when combat was downplayed and crinos was discouraged.<br /> <br /> I suspect their might be some stuff we're not seeing behind closed doors. The art scandal stuff has almost certainly resulted in some phone conferences and some people not getting contracted for m5. This is probably very irritating to Paradox as they're probably aware burning down the old lore alienated a lot if people and they still got in trouble anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-17-2023, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T18:35:06-07:00","id":1518339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518094#post1518094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a follow up to that.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1326\" height=\"191\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8xff6sv.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>So, ignoring concepts created by the scenario they are working on as the corporate wolf, aristocrat wolf, samurai wolf etc. Damm, Francesco it's a lupus werewolf BSD and a Pentex Board Director!!\u200b Like, &quot;let's throw away this concepts which the IP create and stabilished, and back to something everybody already does.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T04:59:02-07:00","id":1518352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518339#post1518339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ignoring concepts created by the scenario they are working on as the corporate wolf, aristocrat wolf, samurai wolf etc. Damm, Francesco it's a lupus werewolf BSD and a Pentex Board Director!!\u200b Like, &quot;let's throw away this concepts which the IP create and stabilished, and back to something everybody already does.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem to be focusing on what a 'base' werewolf is. The problem is that they've done nothing to ACTUALLY make W5 match the typical movie werewolf at all. Never mind using any of the folklore methods, most of which WtA has not even used. You cannot do a version of Howling OR American Werewolf in London in W5 anymore than you can in W20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T06:45:27-07:00","id":1518355,"title":"","content":"The comparison to vampires doesn't really hold up in the first place. Sure, there are plenty of vampire myths and pop-culture you can link to Clans in VtM but over the years even VtM has developed its own brand of what constitutes a &quot;vampire&quot;. Like, a Salubri is a VtM-thing. Besides it doesn't matter anyway. You can point out that there aren't a lot of original stories and myths out there with something like an &quot;aristocrat werewolf&quot;, for example, but the Silver Fangs are still in the game. That WtA is so very different from the original werewolf-mythology was always something that made it more intriguing for me. But that's just me. And the thing is... if you then want to push this thing back to a more basic idea of what a werewolf is then of course most of the setting will just seem like hurdles and obstructions in making this happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T08:21:21-07:00","id":1518360,"title":"","content":"Like they basically didn't want to do a Werewolf: The Apocalypse game, but it was the assignment that they were given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T20:13:45-07:00","id":1518603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518360#post1518360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like they basically didn't want to do a Werewolf: The Apocalypse game, but it was the assignment that they were given.</div> </div> </div> </div>A LOT of how WoD5 has been going seems like Paradox want to use the World of Darkness license to make money, but resent everything they inherited about the games. They want to exploit the brand, but not anything contained therein.<br /> <br /> It's why H5 dispensed with anything having to do with the Imbued. Or why V5 fixated so much on getting back to &quot;the game's roots&quot;. You know, back when Vampire was mostly undefined and mysterious. Where all the maps said &quot;Here Be Dragons&quot;. A setting where all the established politics and players were swept away, so nothing could get in the way of the New Vision^TM.<br /> <br /> Now we see W5, where established relationships and lore are freely ignored. As demonstrated in the thread by the writer from the Hunters Entertainment attempt at W5, where the editor basically said (paraphrasing) &quot;the Sword of Heimdal were purged? I'll pretend I didn't hear that. We should ignore the lore, I want my Nazi Fenrir.&quot;<br /> <br /> Over and over, we see the folks at Paradox seem to come into the projects with their own ideas about what WoD should be. Anything that interferes with this is burned to the ground, to make room for THEIR contributions. A slash-and-burn approach to stewarding a beloved franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T22:49:21-07:00","id":1518611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518603#post1518603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, back when Vampire was mostly undefined and mysterious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strangely enough, Vampire: The Masquarade was <i>very clear</i> about the origin of vampires, their powers and weaknesses<br /> Caine, 2nd, 3rd Generation to present day fledgelings, Camarilla and we are all good<br /> In first edition, Golconda was portrayed as an unadulterated good, and relatively easy to achieve (to the point, Chicago by Night has at least two characters in Golconda, one of whom achieved it in <i>less than a century</i>).<br /> And the &quot;good guy&quot; vampires, aka. Heroes with Fangs was the common, not to mention the whole Crossover-friendlyness<br /> With the second and revised editions World of Darkness became progressively... darker and the various clan myths, origins, etc slowly replaced all those things<br /> I wouldn't be upset if [anything]5 would have gone back to those roots, but where they went is NOT &quot;the game's roots&quot; in my humble opinion<br /> As you wrote Paradox want to use the World of Darkness license to make money<br /> Just they are horrible in it..<br /> You can't change an almost three decade old setting overnight and call it the same! It took time and slow changes to get from 1st ed to V/WW/M/C/W20<br /> The 5th is so different you bascially could call it a different game and you would be right, only World of Darkness <i>in name </i>and everyone knows it<br /> <br /> #NotMyFenris<br /> Mark my word, this whouls thing, it will be disastrous and a colossal faliure!<br /> You can't alienate your old playerbase who expect World of Darkness from... well... World of Darkness and can't lure in new players if you straight up lies to them and selling snake oil.<br /> The future is not bright","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-23-2023, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T23:46:12-07:00","id":1518612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518611#post1518611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strangely enough, Vampire: The Masquarade was <i>very clear</i> about the origin of vampires, their powers and weaknesses<br /> Caine, 2nd, 3rd Generation to present day fledgelings, Camarilla and we are all good<br /> In first edition, Golconda was portrayed as an unadulterated good, and relatively easy to achieve (to the point, Chicago by Night has at least two characters in Golconda, one of whom achieved it in <i>less than a century</i>).<br /> And the &quot;good guy&quot; vampires, aka. Heroes with Fangs was the common, not to mention the whole Crossover-friendlyness<br /> With the second and revised editions World of Darkness became progressively... darker and the various clan myths, origins, etc slowly replaced all those things<br /> I wouldn't be upset if [anything]5 would have gone back to those roots, but where they went is NOT &quot;the game's roots&quot; in my humble opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that most of the VtM part of the World of Darkness hadn't been fleshed out yet. We didn't know who all ran the various cities, how the Camarilla/Anarchs/Sabbat was structured, who the great Methuselahs were and what their plans are, etc. We had the possible origin with Caine, we had Golconda, we have the conflict between the young and the old, and that was about it. A lot of what VtM fans see as staples of the franchise hadn't been written yet.<br /> <br /> THIS is what Paradox wanted to emulate about early VtM. The &quot;blank slate&quot; nature of it.<br /> <br /> Because if it's a blank slate, that means V5's writers could inject all of their ideas into VtM. All they had to do was burn the setting to the ground. Clear away all the brush, as it were. In so doing, making the world seem bigger and more mysterious.<br /> <br /> But they killed so many characters - under the pretense of letting PCs fill the void effortlessly - it made the world seem empty and small. They folded so many options into one another - under the pretense of making it easier for new players - they deprived you of meaningful choices (and watered down the choices you did get). Pruning Bloodlines and Disciplines in a militant crusade against &quot;redundancy&quot;, when that was never a problem.<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn't make the World of Darkness more interesting. Instead it <i>flattens</i> the setting. Makes it more shallow. In the name of making the game approachable, it removes so much messy nuance that could be used to attract people. A fully generic game about supernaturals living in an urban fantasy setting is less captivating that the Classic WoD's <i>fractal specificity</i>.<br /> <br /> You can play a vampire in a lot of roleplaying games now. You can't play a flesh-crafting mystic seeking visceral enlightenment anywhere but VtM.<br /> <br /> You can play a werewolf in a lot of roleplaying games now. You can't play a Garou Viking fighting for Gaia against Entropy and Capitalism anywhere but WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T03:12:39-07:00","id":1518623,"title":"","content":"Pretty much yeah, you can see them running into trouble as early as v5 Anarch were it becomes clear they don't really have any ideas on what to do with the brave new world. It got worse with Sabbat were it becomes clear they can't/wont even re integrate older ideas.<br /> <br /> The only people who've done anything at all with the setting are oynx path and even then cults of the blood gods is a retread parts of states of grace but better and a surprisingly good compromise between stripping down and older lore that is clan heceta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-23-2023, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T03:32:33-07:00","id":1518626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518603#post1518603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A LOT of how WoD5 has been going seems like Paradox want to use the World of Darkness license to make money, but resent everything they inherited about the games. They want to exploit the brand, but not anything contained therein..</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine as IP owners or their creative teams have to do something invigorating to attract new audiences, whilst maintaining the integrity of the lore.<br /> <br /> This sounds sadly like Paradox missed the commercial objective - you either utilise the IPs background lore (which has allowed it to survive for 30 years) and fanbase or you scrap it and start again, in which case it isn\u2019t WTA.<br /> <br /> The cardinal sin is trying to use somethings name but do something completely new, it\u2019s been proven to fail countless times with movie reboots that have strayed too far from their background &amp; in this case it appears disingenuous.<br /> <br /> Commercially there\u2019s no such thing as having your cake and eat it, professional people would have put aside personal objections and review what\u2019s the best way of leveraging the franchise to meet all of the objectives.<br /> <br /> They appear to have failed to do this, which sadly if several threads on this forum are to go by means that W5 will be a commercial failure.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong this sadly happens across numerous industries where egos and vanity concepts over-ride what success looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T03:53:30-07:00","id":1518628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518623#post1518623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much yeah, you can see them running into trouble as early as v5 Anarch were it becomes clear they don't really have any ideas on what to do with the brave new world. It got worse with Sabbat were it becomes clear they can't/wont even re integrate older ideas.<br /> <br /> The only people who've done anything at all with the setting are oynx path and even then cults of the blood gods is a retread parts of states of grace but better and a surprisingly good compromise between stripping down and older lore that is clan heceta.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in hindsight it was the V5 Sabbat book where the issues crystallized for the direction WOD5E was headed into post-V5-controversy, I think. That book was not interested in the old lore or appealing to older fans who had come to look at Sabbat as this expansive concept that eventually even turned into a player-option. But the book was also not invested in creating new lore, let alone addressing the things established by the V5 corebook in a satisfactory manner. You'd think that with the Beckoning and Gehenna War being these two big new lore-ideas of V5 the Sabbat book would expand on that. Instead, we got this muddled, barebones presentation that was different from previous lore and yet didn't establish an interesting identity of its own.<br /> <br /> That sort of set the tone going forward. Even with H5 you'd think that even if you want to completely ignore the Imbued the new concept that was very central to V5, the Second Inquisition, would take center-stage. Instead, once again the program was to ditch the old lore and half-heartedly deal with the new lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T04:22:17-07:00","id":1518631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518626#post1518626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They appear to have failed to do this, which sadly if several threads on this forum are to go by means that W5 will be a commercial failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does remain to be seen. There are very different schools of thought in different spaces. They are trying to animate a new crowd and appeal to people who didn't know or like Werewolf before. Even here you'll hear a lot of praise for some decisions W5 did, especially from folks who didn't like how Werewolf interacted with other splats or some of the setting elements.<br /> <br /> Here the consensus seems to be negative, but reddit is more balanced (even though predominantly negative). Twitter goes between hating the caricature of WtA's worst hits and lambasting Paradox. Rpg.net is more balanced, but very negative about Paradox missteps. On the other hand the official Discord is generally positive and stoked for Werewolf and believes this will be the best Werewolf ever.<br /> <br /> How this translates into sales will really depend on actual sales. If the game gets good buzz and sales it will become the dominant form of Werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T04:50:55-07:00","id":1518632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518631#post1518631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> . On the other hand the official Discord is generally positive and stoked for Werewolf and believes this will be the best Werewolf ever.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Discord mods are draconian about critical statements and wrongfun so should be taken with a pinch of salt since concensus is rigged<br /> I also I've seen some 'interesting' takes from them such people who like older editions are just bigots and trolls which I'm not even sure how to reply to without appearing mean So I'll just comment were in real trouble as a fandom of they're the norm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CUH9TDSO5es\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CUH9TDSO5es\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CUH9TDSO5es\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/CUH9TDSO5es </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-23-2023, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T05:01:59-07:00","id":1518633,"title":"","content":"Spaced did make me giggle, haven't seen that in ages!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T07:15:36-07:00","id":1518638,"title":"","content":"Aside from the MASSIVE Fenrir kerfluffle which does actually explain the reason they are not playable, I just can't help but think WoD5's flattening is doing the exact opposite of what WoD was made for.<br /> <br /> I mean, you are playing a monster and the game is about WHO you are and WHY you are a monster and most importantly; Are you actually the true monster here? That is why Sabbat and the Society of Leopold had a place as PCs, because there was no one answer to the question. It is even MORE muddled with WtA where each tribes has its own take on the litany, there are stolen moons and ronin etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> WoD5 denying anyone but the main focus of the spotlight is outright telling you who is in the right. It is like a scene in the Goblins webcomic, which was made to shine a light on how players treat goblins in DnD, casting detect evil spell and telling their allies killing foes is fine since they are evil. Complete flip of the point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T11:20:19-07:00","id":1518651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518638#post1518638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the MASSIVE Fenrir kerfluffle which does actually explain the reason they are not playable, I just can't help but think WoD5's flattening is doing the exact opposite of what WoD was made for.<br /> <br /> I mean, you are playing a monster and the game is about WHO you are and WHY you are a monster and most importantly; Are you actually the true monster here? That is why Sabbat and the Society of Leopold had a place as PCs, because there was no one answer to the question. It is even MORE muddled with WtA where each tribes has its own take on the litany, there are stolen moons and ronin etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> WoD5 denying anyone but the main focus of the spotlight is outright telling you who is in the right. It is like a scene in the Goblins webcomic, which was made to shine a light on how players treat goblins in DnD, casting detect evil spell and telling their allies killing foes is fine since they are evil. Complete flip of the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get as antagonists don't really fit into this but with JA we know what his paradigm for reworking the WOD-splats was:<ul><li>There are bad-guy factions (Nephandi, Sabbat, BSD etc.) which are bad.</li> <li>Every faction that is upholding the status-quo is also bad (Camarilla, Garou-Nation, hunter-orgs etc.).</li> <li>The factions that want to change the status-quo actually <i>can </i>do good but they can accidentally also do bad things (Anarchs, local Hunter-cells, young Garou etc.).</li> </ul>The only moral grey area in this conception was whether the faction that would be fighting against the status-quo actually made things better. But that's about it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T02:26:38-07:00","id":1518748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518651#post1518651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Get as antagonists don't really fit into this but with JA we know what his paradigm for reworking the WOD-splats was:<ul><li>There are bad-guy factions (Nephandi, Sabbat, BSD etc.) which are bad.</li> <li>Every faction that is upholding the status-quo is also bad (Camarilla, Garou-Nation, hunter-orgs etc.).</li> <li>The factions that want to change the status-quo actually <i>can </i>do good but they can accidentally also do bad things (Anarchs, local Hunter-cells, young Garou etc.).</li> </ul>The only moral grey area in this conception was whether the faction that would be fighting against the status-quo actually made things better. But that's about it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lazyness of a one size fits all for the splats aside (the Sabbat are boy scouts compared to the Nephandi) it doesn't work very well. Pretty much all the status quo changing groups are vaguely defined and decentralised for example the anarchs have never really established any meaningful idea of how to avoid elder obligarchy and tend to be genrally repulsive on their own terms.<br /> <br /> the young garou dynamic frankly is unlikely to work Werewolves only last 80 years and genrally don't so the garou nation older wolves are either fading or have to be fading and incredibly stupid since the system would have been failing well before 2023 making the conflict artificial If you wanted to do that with werewolf it should have been better to do conservatives vs reformists (not left vs right) within a struggling garou nation and have the power struggle cross generational. Probably build some actual political conflict points into it (humanism vs misanthropy, kinfolk rights, metis rights, rebuilding relations with other fera etc) giving players plenty to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-25-2023, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T02:44:27-07:00","id":1518749,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Werewolf never really had a &quot;generational&quot; conflict. Werewolves tend not to live too long, and in the prior editions most of the high ranking werewolves were younger than 50 or so. In W5 it's likely that most of the &quot;older&quot; werewolves at the local caern are going to be Gen X or older Millennials in their early 40's. I guess there is a certain meta element to this, since most of the older werewolf players, who were familiar with the older editions, are members of Gen X or older Millennials - which means they're basically these old, out-of-touch people that have destroyed the world and need to get tossed out and taught lessons by the young kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T04:34:37-07:00","id":1518750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518748#post1518748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lazyness of a one size fits all for the splats aside (the Sabbat are boy scouts compared to the Nephandi) it doesn't work very well. Pretty much all the status quo changing groups are vaguely defined and decentralised for example the anarchs have never really established any meaningful idea of how to avoid elder obligarchy and tend to be genrally repulsive on their own terms.<br /> <br /> the young garou dynamic frankly is unlikely to work Werewolves only last 80 years and genrally don't so the garou nation older wolves are either fading or have to be fading and incredibly stupid since the system would have been failing well before 2023 making the conflict artificial If you wanted to do that with werewolf it should have been better to do conservatives vs reformists (not left vs right) within a struggling garou nation and have the power struggle cross generational. Probably build some actual political conflict points into it (humanism vs misanthropy, kinfolk rights, metis rights, rebuilding relations with other fera etc) giving players plenty to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interesting thing about the generational conflict in W5 is that it actually comes up in Sambrano's latest post. It's the first KM-post about the Get where he seems to respond to the idea of what if at least the younger Get aren't Nazis. So it seems like the generational conflict was more like a compromise-position to lessen the heavy-handed sweeping changes that KM aimed for. Killing off the Younger Brother Tribe, turning the Get into Nazis... I don't even wanna know, I think, what his take on the other Tribes was when that's how he approached &quot;updating&quot; those two Tribes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T04:51:23-07:00","id":1518751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518748#post1518748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably build some actual political conflict points into it (humanism vs misanthropy, kinfolk rights, metis rights, rebuilding relations with other fera etc) giving players plenty to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would have been great and sounds like a big missed opportunity to create the new phase of WTA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T04:54:26-07:00","id":1518752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518749#post1518749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Werewolf never really had a &quot;generational&quot; conflict. Werewolves tend not to live too long, and in the prior editions most of the high ranking werewolves were younger than 50 or so. In W5 it's likely that most of the &quot;older&quot; werewolves at the local caern are going to be Gen X or older Millennials in their early 40's. I guess there is a certain meta element to this, since most of the older werewolf players, who were familiar with the older editions, are members of Gen X or older Millennials - which means they're basically these old, out-of-touch people that have destroyed the world and need to get tossed out and taught lessons by the young kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a certain irony in making the characters we played and portrayed into the enemies of the next generation of players. Almost as if they care more about the clash of player generations than Garou generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T07:34:41-07:00","id":1518757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518749#post1518749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Werewolf never really had a &quot;generational&quot; conflict. Werewolves tend not to live too long, and in the prior editions most of the high ranking werewolves were younger than 50 or so. In W5 it's likely that most of the &quot;older&quot; werewolves at the local caern are going to be Gen X or older Millennials in their early 40's. I guess there is a certain meta element to this, since most of the older werewolf players, who were familiar with the older editions, are members of Gen X or older Millennials - which means they're basically these old, out-of-touch people that have destroyed the world and need to get tossed out and taught lessons by the young kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, in our real world, Baby Boomers are still largely in power.<br /> <br /> Which only goes to show how high Garou mortality is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T08:31:21-07:00","id":1518759,"title":"","content":"One of the elements that makes the Fall of the Nation seem less like a tragedy and more of a good thing is how the previews hint that there was no meaningful loss. The young garou returned their normal lives and the elders only remember an idealized version. Losing Caerns and connection to the umbra seems like an afterthought.<br /> <br /> The reason it bothers me, is that this would mean BSDs and other Wyrmy things would no longer feel like they have to hide as much. Even IF this is a reboot, with the Nation gone the BSDs shouldn't feel pressured to build underground Hives anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T08:35:11-07:00","id":1518760,"title":"","content":"We don't know anything about the BSD's in W5, though. For the big bads of the game they have gotten very little in the previews, except for they exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T08:55:48-07:00","id":1518761,"title":"","content":"A strange thing with the development here is that Karim Muammar was trying to push the idea that the new main-antagonist is Get-Nazis - and you still have that in the second version. But to Justin Achilli the main-antagonist is Pentex instead. Not the Pentex of old, of course, but he talked about them being avatars of greet and endless consumption (there's also the time where he said that the write-up of an evil Formori-lobbyist was his favorite part of the antagonist-section). And this variant-cover they had for the Spanish version which is about Pentex hints that that's probably what this version of W5 will be focusing on. This is also in line with there being less of a focus on the Umbra. Of course, it's a bit weird that the Get-Nazis are still part of this version as well.<br /> <br /> But it seems to me like neither of them liked the idea of the &quot;war against the Wyrm&quot; very much. In both cases, it's about redirecting the focus on who the main-antagonist is. But the Wyrm is still part of the setting at the same time. And we've seen three Tribe-sections where &quot;Gaia dead/dying, Garou-Nation sundered&quot; didn't get a lot of attention - even though these should represent massive shifts for Garou-society.<br /> <br /> It's just... I don't know. Maybe all this will seem more coherent once we can read the book back to back. But with all the previews we've gotten, I could never shake the feeling that all these bits and pieces just don't seem to fit together very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T09:09:31-07:00","id":1518763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518761#post1518761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just... I don't know. Maybe all this will seem more coherent once we can read the book back to back. But with all the previews we've gotten, I could never shake the feeling that all these bits and pieces just don't seem to fit together very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>After H5, I'm pretty sure the idea is to stick the ideas you feel cool and leave it as open ended as possible for people to fill in the blanks with whatever they want them to be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T09:41:17-07:00","id":1518765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518763#post1518763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After H5, I'm pretty sure the idea is to stick the ideas you feel cool and leave it as open ended as possible for people to fill in the blanks with whatever they want them to be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things people said in defence of H5 was that in that case the WOD-team was rushed because they had to get to W5. If W5 ends up having the same strange, incoherent worldbuilding then worldbuilding will wildly swing between &quot;This is how it is. Deal with it.&quot; and open-ended &quot;Who knows why it's like that. You go figure it out.&quot; . In the case of the former, H5, though, was way too controlling (like the idea that hunter-orgs and everybody who's working for them is bad) whereas with the latter there's so little worldbuilding as to be pretty much non-existent (like why are there five Creeds, why did mortal Hunters all over the world start talking about &quot;Reckoning&quot; as some sort of secret handshake...).<br /> <br /> Hopefully, W5 won't be like that... emphasis on &quot;hopefully&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T09:54:29-07:00","id":1518766,"title":"","content":"I think that a quote from Muamar that was shared by James speaks volumes about their design philosophy. They say that they want games with as little fuss and as low maintenance as possible. The whole idea that they'd need to consult someone when doing supplements is against what they are trying to achieve right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"