te\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518751#post1518751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would have been great and sounds like a big missed opportunity to create the new phase of WTA.</div> </div> </div> </div>This type of thing don't give problem?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T11:35:48-07:00","id":1518770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518766#post1518766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a quote from Muamar that was shared by James speaks volumes about their design philosophy. They say that they want games with as little fuss and as low maintenance as possible. The whole idea that they'd need to consult someone when doing supplements is against what they are trying to achieve right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they've failed, 5th edition often vague and lackd clarity in terms of both mechanics and lore this lays it on the players and gm to do the work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-27-2023, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T14:18:13-07:00","id":1518777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518768#post1518768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This type of thing don't give problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>The introduction of new dynamics to tribal structures, a political element to the Garou Nation - if handled or written badly of course, but we are talking about fiction.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s the same for most things in modern content if handled insensitively or lazily, modern writers with access to so many good reference points, resources and aids at the touch of a button have no excuses for handling things badly or creating bad fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T15:51:15-07:00","id":1518784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518777#post1518777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The introduction of new dynamics to tribal structures, a political element to the Garou Nation - if handled or written badly of course, but we are talking about fiction.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s the same for most things in modern content if handled insensitively or lazily, modern writers with access to so many good reference points, resources and aids at the touch of a button have no excuses for handling things badly or creating bad fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems worse to me when you say &quot;no excuse&quot;, as far as I know D&amp;D had a similar problem with hybrids anyway, I don't know if well written helps in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T12:47:34-07:00","id":1518839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518761#post1518761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A strange thing with the development here is that Karim Muammar was trying to push the idea that the new main-antagonist is Get-Nazis - and you still have that in the second version. But to Justin Achilli the main-antagonist is Pentex instead. Not the Pentex of old, of course, but he talked about them being avatars of greet and endless consumption (there's also the time where he said that the write-up of an evil Formori-lobbyist was his favorite part of the antagonist-section). And this variant-cover they had for the Spanish version which is about Pentex hints that that's probably what this version of W5 will be focusing on. This is also in line with there being less of a focus on the Umbra. Of course, it's a bit weird that the Get-Nazis are still part of this version as well.<br /> <br /> But it seems to me like neither of them liked the idea of the &quot;war against the Wyrm&quot; very much. In both cases, it's about redirecting the focus on who the main-antagonist is. But the Wyrm is still part of the setting at the same time. And we've seen three Tribe-sections where &quot;Gaia dead/dying, Garou-Nation sundered&quot; didn't get a lot of attention - even though these should represent massive shifts for Garou-society.<br /> <br /> It's just... I don't know. Maybe all this will seem more coherent once we can read the book back to back. But with all the previews we've gotten, I could never shake the feeling that all these bits and pieces just don't seem to fit together very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I vehemently hate about this upcoming &quot;Werewolf&quot; 5. <br /> <br /> You can just tell that the current overall X5 team didn't or just simply cannot understand the spiritualism that was REALLY important to Werewolf. They'd rather destructure and emplace a cold-iron modernism in Werewolf, where the stereotype of the Garou being &quot;Captain Planeteers&quot; prevails over the setting and nothing else, than the high fantastical aspects seekings of wisdom or razor-jarring battles in the Umbra that Werewolf could reach toward. Now we just get this milquetoast version of the Umbra / Spirit Wilds that's just pure a## to interact with from a mechanical and setting standpoint, from the tidbits of information we got released concerning it. <br /> <br /> I just think it speaks toward how little they cared about Werewolf going into this, and the leaked conversations we can glean from this Indigenous author, who for a short time worked for Paradox, really throws a bone of evidence to them not caring about the Werewolf setting at all.<br /> <br /> Everything Paradox thinks they know about this game comes from pure stereotypes from ignorant detractors; or worse, some of these detractors (who I won't say because I'll probably get my post banned or deleted) who now get to directly work on the it due to Paradox, can now fully realize those stereotypes to fit their past contrivances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T15:21:59-07:00","id":1518851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518839#post1518839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> or worse, some of these detractors (who I won't say because I'll probably get my post banned or deleted) who now get to directly work on the it due to Paradox, can now fully realize those stereotypes to fit their past contrivances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> please don't tell me Lashet is part of the W5 team (though that would explain a lot)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T17:51:35-07:00","id":1518857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyre