've been there on and off for a fair while and it has kinda always been like that, I'm trying calm placid engagement to see if we can have a normal human conversation...not holding out much hope but we'll see...theres some good folks on there but they tend to be the quiet ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 07-27-2023, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T18:03:16-07:00","id":1518859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518851#post1518851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> please don't tell me Lashet is part of the W5 team (though that would explain a lot)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe if you go to the first post in this thread you will find your reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T19:33:22-07:00","id":1518867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518770#post1518770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then they've failed, 5th edition often vague and lackd clarity in terms of both fluff and lore this lays it on the players and gm to do the work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that depends on whether that meant low maintenance for players or low maintenance for them. I have a sneaking suspicion he was referring to the latter. Probably wanting nothing more than churning out a Rulebook, some basic supplements and a few modules before moving onto the next line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T23:13:12-07:00","id":1518872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518839#post1518839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just tell that the current overall X5 team didn't or just simply cannot understand the spiritualism that was REALLY important to Werewolf. They'd rather destructure and emplace a <b>cold-iron modernism</b> in Werewolf, where the stereotype of the Garou being &quot;Captain Planeteers&quot; prevails over the setting and nothing else, than the high fantastical aspects seekings of wisdom or razor-jarring battles in the Umbra that Werewolf could reach toward. Now we just get this milquetoast version of the Umbra / Spirit Wilds that's just pure a## to interact with from a mechanical and setting standpoint, from the tidbits of information we got released concerning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cold-iron modernism is the part that most bothers me. Tooting my own horn here, because I grew up with the ragged remnants of animism my ancestors had and WtA just fit perfectly into it. I understood even as a 14-year-old the whole 'you treat something badly and it will give that back at you'-theme.<br /> <br /> That and the modernism is extremely blind considering that not everyone lives in the city or WANTS to live in the city. WtA was one of the games that offered a lot of non-urban stuff to do and that constantly reminded the players that nature was not something 'out there' but part of everyday life.<br /> <br /> And if they removed the animism due to not wanting to anger Indigenous folks? Then they are ignoring that animism is found outside those circles as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T23:57:39-07:00","id":1518878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518872#post1518872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cold-iron modernism is the part that most bothers me. Tooting my own horn here, because I grew up with the ragged remnants of animism my ancestors had and WtA just fit perfectly into it. I understood even as a 14-year-old the whole 'you treat something badly and it will give that back at you'-theme.<br /> <br /> That and the modernism is extremely blind considering that not everyone lives in the city or WANTS to live in the city. WtA was one of the games that offered a lot of non-urban stuff to do and that constantly reminded the players that nature was not something 'out there' but part of everyday life.<br /> <br /> And if they removed the animism due to not wanting to anger Indigenous folks? Then they are ignoring that animism is found outside those circles as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when you put that in the context of how the previews from last October described the relationship between spirits and Garou. The example there was how Garou can't tell the difference between a Wyld-spirit and a Wyrm-spirit and they have to investigate the spirit first to determine what its deal is. But that's such a &quot;science-based&quot; idea of how you deal with spirits, like the main-thing is about empirical analysis. There's nothing spiritual about it as to focus on being connected to the spirits and communicating with them or animistic as in the land, people and spirits being connected to each other. It's weird that in this conception the Garou might have more supernatural tools with their Gifts but overall, their way to figure out a spirit is pretty much the same as what a mortal Hunter would choose to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T01:43:21-07:00","id":1518887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518867#post1518867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that depends on whether that meant low maintenance for players or low maintenance for them. I have a sneaking suspicion he was referring to the latter. Probably wanting nothing more than churning out a Rulebook, some basic supplements and a few modules before moving onto the next line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that was clearly the initial plan. Which is frankly a very odd mindset for a game designed for new players, basic learning principles are often not in place in the core books such as cognitive load, accesability of work or clarity of writting.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting the game often contradicts it's own proposed objectives, for example disciplines and feeding are actually more complex than previous editions In v5 and additional rules such as humours, touchstones and clan compulsions. A friend of mine suggested that 5th edition isn't so much designed to be user friendly but to shape how new players engage with the game and enforce private quirks of the games designers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-02-2023, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T06:12:59-07:00","id":1518927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518784#post1518784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems worse to me when you say &quot;no excuse&quot;, as far as I know D&amp;D had a similar problem with hybrids anyway, I don't know if well written helps in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm saying with the resources at hand there's no excuse for lazy or insensitive writing, I am also saying that writers can deal with some difficult subjects in a mature appropriate way, again it isn't difficult now to watch a creative writing course or cultural lecture on Youtube (just need to select a credible one, the latter usually via speakers from the culture).<br /> <br /> Will a writer please everybody no and thats not a new phenomena (just a wider and quicker reaction), but given the resources to hand they can create a good product that meets approval of the majority of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T07:58:25-07:00","id":1518933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518927#post1518927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I'm saying with the resources at hand there's no excuse for lazy or insensitive writing, I am also saying that writers can deal with some difficult subjects in a mature appropriate way, again it isn't difficult now to watch a creative writing course or cultural lecture on Youtube (just need to select a credible one, the latter usually via speakers from the culture).<br /> <br /> Will a writer please everybody no and thats not a new phenomena (just a wider and quicker reaction), but given the resources to hand they can create a good product that meets approval of the majority of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my life experience, laziness is justifiable with the concept that a job well done will yield me the same as an average job, the difference is that one of the two is more tiring, and using Youtube reference doesn't go well, because anyone can post a video and as long as he knows how to speak well he can convince you that false information is true and even if it is not the case, in the end it doesn't necessarily is enough after all writing is an art. After that nowadays companies as a general rule, are not concerned about addressing sensitive subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T09:00:10-07:00","id":1518936,"title":"","content":"And consider that you expand your best ideas into a product whose profits go to another person who has written anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T09:30:53-07:00","id":1518937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518933#post1518933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my life experience, laziness is justifiable with the concept that a job well done will yield me the same as an average job, the difference is that one of the two is more tiring, and using Youtube reference doesn't go well, because anyone can post a video and as long as he knows how to speak well he can convince you that false information is true and even if it is not the case, in the end it doesn't necessarily is enough after all writing is an art. After that nowadays companies as a general rule, are not concerned about addressing sensitive subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and Youtube is just an example not to be taken too literally, my point is still that writers have access to resources, peer review and networking which they've never had before.<br /> <br /> Agreed laziness is prevalent amongst many many industries for the reasons you've mentioned, however an average job in this context may have damaged the commercial success of the project (may have, as others have pointed out that remains to be seen with its sales). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T23:50:13-07:00","id":1519564,"title":"","content":"I feel like there's a certain hypocritical irony in declaring all Fenrir as Nazis in an edition where we are actively avoiding reducing tribes down to their ethnic components.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12752-mist-walker","name":"Mist-Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:23:39-07:00","id":1519598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1518040#post1518040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And silly me belived for three decades, one of the Garou's biggest tragedy was to be fractured in to Tribes with distinct culture and charactersitics and Patrons. This is the source most of their problem, they are not an united people.</div> </div> </div> </div>And silly me believed it was a good enough metaphor about the countries and people of our real world fighting each other and not being able to accept their differences in order to band together to save the world from collapse and entropy... But I suppose since it wasn't explained literally, it was just me believing it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T16:42:46-07:00","id":1519802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut#post1518037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img width=\"666\" height=\"888\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1097953408259985579/1129791524624928928/IMG_0595.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I uhh, what? Not only are ahroun VERY different from the Fenrir, but the Fenrir also are one of the closest to the 'expected' type of werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more I read of the 5th edition stuff, the more I hate it. I have been playing Get and Get adjacent stuff for years. They are incredibly interesting and unique. It's like Jachili say &quot;norse&quot; and thought Nazi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T16:47:50-07:00","id":1519803,"title":"","content":"As for multiple archetypes, someone didn't watch anything by Overly Sarcastic Productions. In one video, Red points out about 13 different werewolf archetypes. from about 20 different myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T07:27:30-07:00","id":1520034,"title":"","content":"I posted this earlier but it got hit by the spam filter bot when I tried to edit it, so I'm gonna repost it...<br /> <br /> I'm not going to mince words here, Justin Achilli has been trying to force everyone to play Vampire the &quot;One True Way&quot; and to tell all naysayers to go play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; since at least 1999 with VTM Revised, but seeing him do the same thing to Werewolf, the game that always presented itself as a game of savage action-horror from the very beginning is just baffling.<br /> <br /> You'd think Achilli would pass on Werewolf and try to tackle Wraith 5E instead (or at least Mage since that one was more popular) but him, Kareem, and the rest of the Paradox/Renegade crew doing this to Werewolf feels especially vindictive.<br /> <br /> I don't know what they were thinking when they decided to let Achilli do Werewolf. You think Paradox would've gotten someone like Ethan Skemp to head up W5 instead but I guess not.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T07:55:23-07:00","id":1520036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520034#post1520034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this earlier but it got hit by the spam filter bot when I tried to edit it, so I'm gonna repost it...<br /> <br /> I'm not going to mince words here, Justin Achilli has been trying to force everyone to play Vampire the &quot;One True Way&quot; and to tell all naysayers to go play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; since at least 1999 with VTM Revised, but seeing him do the same thing to Werewolf, the game that always presented itself as a game of savage action-horror from the very beginning is just baffling.<br /> <br /> You'd think Achilli would pass on Werewolf and try to tackle Wraith 5E instead (or at least Mage since that one was more popular) but him, Kareem, and the rest of the Paradox/Renegade crew doing this to Werewolf feels especially vindictive.<br /> <br /> I don't know what they were thinking when they decided to let Achilli do Werewolf. You think Paradox would've gotten someone like Ethan Skemp to head up W5 instead but I guess not.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The really bad thing is that of the two Developers Achilli was the one who disliked WtA the least based on the communications we saw from Karim to the HE writers, I mean when your writers are having to explain basic background lore and setting info to the Developers more than a year into development you know something is deeply wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T08:21:57-07:00","id":1520038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520034#post1520034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd think Achilli would pass on Werewolf and try to tackle Wraith 5E instead (or at least Mage since that one was more popular) but him, Kareem, and the rest of the Paradox/Renegade crew doing this to Werewolf feels especially vindictive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>no way would he want to do wraith, you exist in an alternate dimension so its not 'street'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T10:07:07-07:00","id":1520044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520038#post1520038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no way would he want to do wraith, you exist in an alternate dimension so its not 'street'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You do have a point there. But there's something about Achilli and his mindset that always kinda rubbed me the wrong way, even when it comes to Vampire, I never agreed with him that much.<br /> <br /> Let's be real here, VTM 1E and 2E were very much the &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas&quot; badwrongfun that Achilli hates and that I personally love. The whole &quot;Storytelling Game of Personal Horror&quot; was largely just a marketing pitch to get goths and drama students into RPG's (said marketing pitch worked like a charm, of course) and some fluff in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Even the Humanity mechanic was just a way of cribbing the Sanity meter from Call of Cthulhu. Mark Rein-Hagen and crew were all about cribbing stuff they liked from other sources in the development of VTM, and not just vampire books and movies, but other tabletop RPG's like D&amp;D, Call of Cthulhu, and Shadowrun (all of which get a shout-out in the back of the 1E corebook)<br /> <br /> There's a lot of unfortunate historical revisionism surrounding Vampire's first edition. It was pure &quot;Vampions&quot; rule of cool badwrongfun from day one with a thin veneer of angst, and that was part of the charm IMHO. And from what I can tell from back in the day, the ideas of &quot;Personal Horror&quot; and &quot;Supers with Fangs&quot; weren't necessarily the mutually exclusive and diamterically opposed concepts they're seen as today. <br /> <br /> Even when you dismiss the more &quot;out there&quot; stuff like <i>Alien Hunger </i>or <i>Awakening: Diablerie Mexico</i>, 1E is the edition that has the most genuinely heroic vampires and the only defined rules for Golconda and Rebirth in the original run of the game. Even the more acclaimed 1E books like <i>Chicago By Night</i> or <i>The Hunters Hunted</i> have stuff that would make the V5 crowd chafe.<br /> <br /> You've got countless historical and mythic figures as vampires in Chicago By Night while The Hunters Hunted has lots of Numina for PC's to use, groups like the Children of Osiris and the Young Bloods, a Penn Jillette expy, a ghoul Puritan super-hunter, and a mage with a faux-Greek name living in New York who consorts with Elves (no joke, one of the allies Arctos has is an Elvish warlord. Look it up)<br /> <br /> If that ain't &quot;gonzo badwrongfun&quot; then I don't know what is!\u200b<br /> <br /> Oft-quoted factoids like &quot;The combat mechanics were designed to be janky on purpose to discourage combat and encourage personal horror&quot; are a pure cope from the likes of the &quot;you're playing the game wrong&quot; crowd.<br /> <br /> The combat mechanics were jank because the game was largely designed by a bunch of amateurs. Mark Rein-Hagen had worked on Ars Magica before but Jonathan Tweet did more of the heavy lifting with that one's design.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the long-winded tirade about Vampire but I think it kind of reinforces the point I made earlier. With the approach Achilli had towards Vampire, you could at least make the argument that he was trying to have the game try and actually back up the fluff found in the original corebook and as much as I detest V5, the line of logic behind that game's drastic changes can at least make sense from that specific argument.<br /> <br /> The approach that Achilli and Muammar have towards Werewolf is just purely vindictive and petty spite towards all the older editions of a great game. After seeing this travesty, I'm gonna stick to W20 or even Werewolf 2E.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Paradox should've just got Ethan Skemp and Joshua Timbrook to do W5 instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T10:39:14-07:00","id":1520046,"title":"","content":"I ponder if Skemp and Timbrook just refused, after the V5 scandals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T16:13:06-07:00","id":1520064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520044#post1520044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the long-winded tirade about Vampire but I think it kind of reinforces the point I made earlier. With the approach Achilli had towards Vampire, you could at least make the argument that he was trying to have the game try and actually back up the fluff found in the original corebook and as much as I detest V5, the line of logic behind that game's drastic changes can at least make sense from that specific argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>In many ways the conversations about the WoD and especially about its metaplot are less conversations about the actual games in WoD and more about Vampire itself and how people know very little about what the other games were actually about. And why there was such an uproar when Mage: Revised came out in the state it did (even if it did get much much better in the latter half).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:45:23-07:00","id":1520124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520034#post1520034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this earlier but it got hit by the spam filter bot when I tried to edit it, so I'm gonna repost it...<br /> <br /> I'm not going to mince words here, Justin Achilli has been trying to force everyone to play Vampire the &quot;One True Way&quot; and to tell all naysayers to go play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; since at least 1999 with VTM Revised, but seeing him do the same thing to Werewolf, the game that always presented itself as a game of savage action-horror from the very beginning is just baffling.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Must say it's fun that despite this attitude, and mind I'm not trying to say that what you wrote is untrue, the revised edition feels like one of the more varied and completed corebooks that white wolf put out.<br /> Let's you play Sabbat, Anarchs, street level stuff, pulp archeological epics, all in one single package. Thirteen clans and minor tidbits that let you play bloodlines too, even if in small capacity. Path of enlightment too. The intros weren't the most evocative but they were very clear to teenage me, and just by those I had a clear grasp of the gameworld.<br /> Really you had the barebones to play almost any style, stuff and thing from the get-go. I always thought it was corebook 101, done right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T11:23:14-07:00","id":1520138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520124#post1520124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Must say it's fun that despite this attitude, and mind I'm not trying to say that what you wrote is untrue, the <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>revised edition</b></span> feels like one of the more varied and completed corebooks that white wolf put out.<br /> Let's you play Sabbat, Anarchs, street level stuff, pulp archeological epics, all in one single package. Thirteen clans and minor tidbits that let you play bloodlines too, even if in small capacity. Path of enlightment too. The intros weren't the most evocative but they were very clear to <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>teenage me</b></span>, and just by those I had a clear grasp of the gameworld.<br /> Really you had the barebones to play almost any style, stuff and thing from the get-go. I always thought it was corebook 101, done right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so old.....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T11:42:16-07:00","id":1520140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520124#post1520124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Must say it's fun that despite this attitude, and mind I'm not trying to say that what you wrote is untrue, the revised edition feels like one of the more varied and completed corebooks that white wolf put out.<br /> Let's you play Sabbat, Anarchs, street level stuff, pulp archeological epics, all in one single package. Thirteen clans and minor tidbits that let you play bloodlines too, even if in small capacity. Path of enlightment too. The intros weren't the most evocative but they were very clear to teenage me, and just by those I had a clear grasp of the gameworld.<br /> Really you had the barebones to play almost any style, stuff and thing from the get-go. I always thought it was corebook 101, done right.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. The Revised corebook was the first version of Masquerade I ever played, right before V20 came out. If you stick to just the corebook, it's perfect without being as bulky as V20.<br /> <br /> Most of the really bad metaplot stuff and Achilli's smarmy attitude came about in the supplements. Literally the only metaplot changes I remember from the Revised corebook were the different Assamite clan weakness and Malkavians getting Dementation by default.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's the OG setting. Gangrel are still listed as a Camarilla clan, the Ravnos are still a major clan and you even get a nice array of NPC's from the other denizens of the World of Darkness emulated via Disciplines while 1e and 2e only had very brief writeups for Lupines and Magi while ghosts and faeries got mentioned but no real stats.<br /> <br /> I do kinda miss the wider variety of human antagonist write-ups in the 1e and 2e cores. IIRC, in Revised you've got an Inquisitor, a Government Agent, and I think there might've been a mafia hitman too.<br /> <br /> Like, if I was going to do a Masquerade game, I'd set it in the late 90's/early 2000's and use the mysterious and brooding setting of 1e and early 2e but the rules of Revised. V20 works well too but if I'm gonna go for the real deal old-school feel, I'll use Revised rules.<br /> <br /> Maybe call that setting riff &quot;Vampire: The New Millennium&quot; or something? It's a slightly tweaked variant of the vanilla Masquerade setting where that late 90's/early 2000's attitude is played up to an over-the-top degree.<br /> <br /> From the release of the 1e corebook until Under A Blood Red Moon, the Vampire metaplot was nonexistent, and from Under A Blood Red Moon to the Revised corebook, the metaplot was pretty much confined to the Chicago Metropolitan Area. Hell, Werewolf and Mage probably had more metaplot in the first two editions than Vampire did and most of that concerned Samuel Haight. <br /> <br /> It wasn't until Guide to the Camarilla, the Clan Novels, and Time of Thin Blood that the metaplot really begins to go out of control for VTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T16:23:45-07:00","id":1520159,"title":"","content":"Interestingly to me, the golden age of Werewolf was Revised. A period where the stakes were high and the world was in a horrible place. The Garou were undermanned and undergunned, yet they had a cause and they could make changes. The whole Nation moving towards goals and allowing players to interact with those goals and the new allies (and playstyles!) that the game brought along. Sure there was a lot of shit to get through, but maybe, just maybe you could do something about it. An especially cool metaplot element was how open the big stories were for player interference and for them to be the big figures in building bridges. It ended off with Apocalypse, a brillliant book that put it quite well what they were fighting and how you could make it your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T19:56:14-07:00","id":1520168,"title":"","content":"This discussion has inspired me to work on a setting riff for V20/Revised called &quot;Vampire: The Millennium Age&quot; that I will post in the VTM forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T00:03:49-07:00","id":1520267,"title":"","content":"Something I've noticed is that w5 get is just v5 sabbat except werewolves. This matches my general feel that w5 is just v5 but werewolves.<br /> <br /> Its all so lazy and unambitious and this is becoming an endemic trait of 5th edition when they're not trying to enforce a style of play they're not doing anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-10-2023, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T00:58:14-07:00","id":1520268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520267#post1520267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've noticed is that w5 get is just v5 sabbat except werewolves. This matches my general feel that w5 is just v5 but werewolves.<br /> <br /> Its all so lazy and unambitious and this is becoming an endemic trait of 5th edition when they're not trying to enforce a style of play they're not doing anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the added bit that at times while the writers are talking about the ills of Garou society and why Garou are so bad for the umpteenth time, they come close to saying &quot;Hmm, maybe... now that I think about it... maybe all Garou are the Sabbat (except the PC-Garou, of course).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T03:18:59-07:00","id":1520278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520268#post1520268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the added bit that at times while the writers are talking about the ills of Garou society and why Garou are so bad for the umpteenth time, they come close to saying &quot;Hmm, maybe... now that I think about it... maybe all Garou are the Sabbat (except the PC-Garou, of course).&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey look, &quot;show, don't tell&quot; it's a difficult thing to do. And it also requires a bare minimum of trust in your readers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T20:07:32-07:00","id":1520352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518037-explanation-why-fenrir-were-cut?p=1520044#post1520044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oft-quoted factoids like &quot;The combat mechanics were designed to be janky on purpose to discourage combat and encourage personal horror&quot; are a pure cope from the likes of the &quot;you're playing the game wrong&quot; crowd.<br /> <br /> The combat mechanics were jank because the game was largely designed by a bunch of amateurs. Mark Rein-Hagen had worked on Ars Magica before but Jonathan Tweet did more of the heavy lifting with that one's design.</div> </div> </div> </div>the mechanics may have been janky, but at least they WORKED. which is more than I can say for the new ones, what 5th edition has is unclear and unusable as all hell. I mean they have been cannibalising CoD to death, they could have at least used it's combat mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}